Error: Jet.RuntimeOnlyAtBuildTime: Compile-time code calls `stamp()` while building, but `#Runtime(.Only)` keeps it to the running program
  --> Tests/UI/runtime_only_called_while_building.jet:6:17
    |
  6 |     value: #run stamp()
    |                 ^^^^^
 Why: `#Runtime(.Only)` marks a function, method or block that runs only in the shipped program, so neither compile-time code inside it nor compile-time code calling it may run while building.
 Fix: Move the compile-time code out of the `#Runtime(.Only)` code, or call it from run-time code. To stop only automatic compile-time evaluation and keep explicit `#run`, use `#Runtime(.NoEager)`.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.RuntimeOnlyAtBuildTime
